# The backfill migrations under backend/migrations/ guard their UPDATEs on
# verbatim instruction/text values that can contain embedded newlines.
# core.autocrlf is commonly true on Windows checkouts, so without this rule a
# CRLF checkout would make Postgres compare "...\r\n..." against a stored
# "...\n...", and a guard would silently match zero rows — never erroring,
# just doing nothing.
*.sql text eol=lf
